        <p>Justices Wills and Charles on Thursday, struck off the rolls Georg. Edward Weare, solicitor, Bristol, convicted and fined for knowingly permitting premises of his to be used as a house of ill-fame. Justice Wills said this amounted to traffic in prostitution, and it was almost an insult to ask the court to allow such a man to remain on the rolls. Justice Charles concurred.</p>
        <p>Mr. W. C. Hargrove, the English owner of a ranche o 60,000 acres at Linares, in Mexico, has been robbed and murdered, it is supposed by servants.</p>
