        <p>PEARSON AND KNOWLES V. BEWSZY FORGE ENGINEERS.— Played on the ground of the first named at Arpley. The , home team were the first to occupy the wickett ; Hamp- son, and Taylor, facing the attack, the score reaching 32 before the farmer was bowled. After Peers had as- sisted in adding 21 runs to the aggregate, Howard joined Taylor' and these two defying the efforts of the bowlers, carried the total to 106, when the innings was declared closed—Taylor carrying out his bat for a splendidly played 56. Beyond some hard hitting by Davey and some good cricket by Thorp the Engineers cut up badly against Beaman and Howard the analysis reading : covers in. runs wkt4. Beaman l2 2 27 5 Howard 6 5 1 3 Hampson PEARSON AND KNOWLES. REWSEY FORGE ENGINEERS. F Taylor not out a Hampson b R Davey l6 T Davey b Hampson G Peers o Armitage B R C Lewis h Beaman Davey 5 R Davey b Beaman 6 F Howard not out EI C Llewellyn b Beaman ... 6 Beaman to bat W Armitage b Beaman ... 0 Thompson „ W Mee b Beaman Plckton /P 7 Hardman b Howard Palmer „ 7 Armitage b Howard 0 Chaslwiek " J Armitage b Howard Gough 9, D Gibson not out 1 1 Extras 8 Extras 5 For 2 wkts.... 106 Total</p>
